        new(82,"PED:US-CCSS-MATH:G2:U06:L01","https://im.kendallhunt.com/k5/teachers/grade-2/unit-6/lesson-1/preparation.html","1ae82372416cc3ef0417ee4add89df805f546e7608781e7e6b5a4b787138734b",
            ["CCSS:2.G.A.1"],
            ["Learning goal: You will recognize and name shapes based on the number of sides and vertices (corners).\nIn previous grades, you identified, described, and compared two-dimensional and three-dimensional shapes. You learned that shapes have defining attributes and drew shapes that possessed these attributes. In this lesson, you learn that you can identify a shape by the number of sides and corners it has.",
             "Key ideas:\n- Recognize triangles, quadrilaterals, pentagons, and hexagons based on the number of sides and vertices (corners)\n- In previous grades, you identified, described, and compared two-dimensional and three-dimensional shapes\n- Use mathematical attributes such as sides, angles, parallelism, or length—not size or orientation—to justify a classification.",
             "Example 1: Sort the shapes into categories in a way that makes sense to you. Be prepared to explain how you sorted the shapes.\nApproach: “What did you notice when you sorted the shapes by the number of corners?” (We didn’t have to do anything. The same shapes are in each group.)\nExample 2: Pick 1 shape card. Be prepared to name and describe your shape to a partner.\nApproach: “What clues did your partner give you that made it easy to guess your shape?” (number of sides, number of corners)",
