             "Key ideas:\n- Describe shapes using defining attributes\n- Draw and name shapes based on defining attributes\n- Use mathematical attributes such as sides, angles, parallelism, or length—not size or orientation—to justify a classification.",
             "Example 1: Find the value of each expression mentally. \\(5 + 30 + 5\\) \\(50 + 30 + 5\\) \\(50 + 5 + 30 + 5\\) \\(500 + 30 + 5\\)\nApproach: “What were some of the different values of 5 in the sums you found?” (5, 50, 500)",
